The patient is a 45-year-old female who developed a skin rash, itching, nausea, and dizziness after starting amoxicillin approximately five days earlier. Symptoms reportedly began around Day -2 and persisted until Day 0. The patient also takes paracetamol as needed.

Amoxicillin is the suspected medicine because the onset and symptoms are compatible with a possible drug-induced hypersensitivity reaction. However, the causal relationship has not been confirmed, and the contribution of other medicines or underlying conditions cannot be excluded.

The patient requires prompt clinical evaluation. Severe dizziness, fainting, breathing difficulty, or swelling of the face, lips, or throat requires emergency medical attention.

**Final assessment:** Suspected amoxicillin-associated adverse drug reaction. Further clinical assessment and medication-history review are required to establish causality and determine seriousness.
